Subj: IBMTOK 2.0(c) submittal
------------------------------------------------------------------
Below is the submittal form for v 2.0(c) of the IBM Token Ring MAC 
driver.  This update is for the Microsoft 2.0 Shrink-Wrap and NDDK 
releases, CS-008.  It fixes a bug in the DOS driver (see below).

------------------------------------------------------------------

DATE: April 24th, 1990

PRODUCT: IBM Token Ring MAC Driver (OS/2 and DOS)

TARGETED FOR DEFINED RELEASE:

    ECO -

    Release - CS-008
        Microsoft 2.0 Shrink-Wrap
        Microsoft 2.0 NDDK

    Update Disk -

FILENAME:           PREVIOUS VERSION:        NEW VERSION:
=========           =================        ============
IBMTOK.OS2              2.0(b)                  2.0(c)
IBMTOK.DOS              2.0(b)                  2.0(c)

LIST OF FILES THAT CHANGED:
        INIT.ASM, EQU.MAC

EXECUTABLE LOCATION: (sharename,pswrd,directory)
        sharename is \\iditerod\ibmtok
        directory is \2.0c
        OS/2 driver is os2\product\ibmtok.os2
        DOS driver is dos\product\ibmtok.dos

SOURCE LOCATION: (sharename,pswrd,directory)
        sharename is \\iditerod\ibmtok
        directory is \2.0c

DATE AND TIME OF EXECUTABLE/FILES:
        OS/2 driver:
            IBMTOK   OS2    17108   4-24-90   2:59p
        DOS driver:
            IBMTOK   DOS     9232   4-24-90   2:58p

CODE AND DATA MEMORY REQUIREMENTS:
        Varies based on parameters.  Using the default parameter values
        approximately 8K.  However, this can increase up to 15K if
        large values are configured for MaxTransmits.  This would normally
        only be used on a heavily loaded server.

DEPENDENCIES AND BUILD INSTRUCTIONS:
        - Tool requirements:
            MAKE    X045
            MASM    5.10
            LINK    5.01.20 or 5.01.21
            MAPSYM  4.00
            EXE2COM a replacement for EXE2BIN which is compatible with
                    any version of DOS in use (use 1.04 or later)

        - Libraries:
            DOSCALLS.LIB    from MASM 5.10 or MSC 5.10 or equivalent
            in INC subdirectory

        - Include files:
            DEVHLP.INC      from OS/2 BAK or DDK
            DOSMAC.INC      from OS/2 BAK or DDK
            DEVSYM.INC      from OS/2 BAK or DDK
            in INC subdirectory

        - Build Instructions:
            1.  Setup T: to a TOOLS sharename (eg. \\SIRIUS\TOOLS)
            2.  Setup G: to a GLOBALS sharename (eg. \\PORSCHE\OS2GLOB)
            3.  Execute MKOS2.BAT or MKDOS.BAT, optionally supplying
                "DEV" (uppercase) as an argument if you want to build
                the development version instead of PRODUCT.
          Note that if you had last built a different version (DEV instead
          of PRODUCT, or DOS instead of OS/2, etc) you will have to do
          something to cause all of the files to be rebuilt before using
          the batch files (e.g. "TOUCH *.ASM" or "DEL *.OBJ").

DESCRIPTION OF CHANGES:

        Change to DOS driver to correct a problem with the code which
        relocates the INIT code out of the way of volatile data structures
        being allocated.  Since the copy operation overlapped the code
        was copied incorrectly, resulting in a crash after load.

REFERENCE BUG NUMBER:
        N/A

CHANGES IMPLEMENTED BY:
        Glenn Connery

KNOWN BUGS (This includes parts of the file or program that have
not been completed):






